 "<code class=\"docstring\">`sym` enters an interactive symbolic simulation mode built on `grind`.\nUnlike `grind =&gt;`, it does not eagerly introduce hypotheses or apply by-contradiction,\ngiving the user explicit control over `intro`, `apply`, and `internalize` steps.\n\nExample:\n```\nexample (x : Nat) : myP x → myQ x := by\n  sym [myP_myQ] =&gt;\n    intro h\n    finish\n```\n</code>",
